### NovaBank Stage 5 — security scenarios through APIM
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or any .http-compatible client).
###
### Demonstrates the four scenarios from the Stage 5 build plan, all through the APIM
### gateway (not direct to the services) — proving APIM's JWT validation and each
### service's own ownership check both actually work end to end.
###
### Uses the Resource Owner Password Credentials (ROPC) grant purely for scripted test
### convenience — never use ROPC in a real application; it's deprecated by Microsoft for
### production use because it trains users to type passwords into arbitrary clients.

@tenantId = 357b06c3-23ee-408a-a70b-57eaddc48aad
@clientId = bf3edf1a-2e04-4794-a3d3-5e516c5321ef
@gateway = https://nb-dev-apim.azure-api.net

@testUser1 = novabank-test1@mibbrahim45gmail.onmicrosoft.com
@testUser1Password = {{$dotenv NOVABANK_TEST1_PASSWORD}}
@testUser1CustomerId = 0b337c49-d82e-4303-8ae6-5cd0daa63a3f

@testUser2CustomerId = ff58781a-7832-43c4-b3db-de1dc4fecdbb

###
# @name tokenFullScope
# Acquires a token for test user 1 with all four scopes consented.
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&client_id={{clientId}}
&username={{testUser1}}
&password={{testUser1Password}}
&scope=api://{{clientId}}/accounts.read api://{{clientId}}/cards.read api://{{clientId}}/cards.write api://{{clientId}}/transfers.write

###
# @name tokenReadOnly
# Acquires a token for the SAME user but requesting only accounts.read — used below to
# prove the "missing scope" scenario (this token genuinely cannot do transfers.write).
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&client_id={{clientId}}
&username={{testUser1}}
&password={{testUser1Password}}
&scope=api://{{clientId}}/accounts.read

###
# Scenario 1: own data works (200)
# test user 1's token, requesting test user 1's own accounts.
GET {{gateway}}/account/api/v1/customers/{{testUser1CustomerId}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenFullScope.response.body.$.access_token}}

###
# Scenario 2: another customer's data returns 404 (not 403 — never confirm the resource
# exists). test user 1's token, requesting test user 2's accounts.
GET {{gateway}}/account/api/v1/customers/{{testUser2CustomerId}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenFullScope.response.body.$.access_token}}

###
# Scenario 3: missing scope returns 403.
# The read-only token has no transfers.write scope — APIM's account-api policy rejects
# this before the request ever reaches account-service.
POST {{gateway}}/account/api/v1/customers/{{testUser1CustomerId}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenReadOnly.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-test-scenario-3

{
  "fromAccountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "toAccountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "amount": 10.00,
  "currency": "AED",
  "narration": "Should be rejected for missing scope"
}

###
# Scenario 4: no token returns 401.
GET {{gateway}}/account/api/v1/customers/{{testUser1CustomerId}}/accounts
